{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-125558",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "A dilation with center at the origin and a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$ can be represented by the function  \n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(\\frac{1}{2}x,\\frac{1}{2}y).\n$$\n\nApplying this function to the point $(8,-4),$ we have\n\n$$\n(8,-4)↦(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-4))=(4,-2).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the resulting point is $(4,-2).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14221848/assets/c2c00f1380ce776da3fe4e1ab2b30c969d5d7436966d907db7a0ceb5f0a13f33.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
